From 2a1c471bafa24cfb28b6da1cb1f31ab7b92415d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:23:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(outcomes): the turn-end refresh names only its own turn's
 evidence, never a snapshot [daveey]

PR1131 review t_01a1d0ca50bdd065 (ce34362731): capture_turn_identity snapshotted every live-turn evidence
the chat held at conclusion, so (1) the TUI refresh, which runs after settle_prompt_state admitted a newer
turn, discounted that newer turn's marker, and (2) the gateway capture discounted a concurrent Desktop
turn's marker while it waited on the gateway's lease.

- hermes_state_outcome.turn_identity(marker=, lease_holder=, gateway_token=) builds the concluding turn's
  identity from handles only that turn holds; capture_turn_identity is gone. Lease token = holder (unique
  per turn: pid+relay turn uuid), gateway token = active_turn_token (uuid per turn).
- agent._last_session_turn_lease_holder: set at lease admission, kept after release (the active attr is
  cleared even when a busy store defers the release).
- TUI: run_body reads its own marker back right after recording it (st.own_marker); the turn-end refresh
  and the refused-turn retry timer pass concluding_turn_identity(agent, own_marker). Nothing passed =
  nothing discounted.
- Gateway: the event's _gateway_active_turn_token (cleared only after the handler returns) and the turn
  agent's lease holder; never a marker.
- tests/tui_gateway/test_update_pause.py: the home fixture keeps card sources local. The turn-end refresh
  now derives past the turn's own marker and reads the chat's cards; with Thread inlined process-wide the
  remote-links worker loop ran forever (CI slice 6, 600 s file timeout at a007a31d and ce34362731).

Tests: test_outcome_late_turn_end_refresh.py covers both review repros (TUI after settle, gateway with a
concurrent TUI marker), late gateway refresh x routing/lease, own-evidence discount on all three paths,
refused-turn timer x routing/lease/marker.
